      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Vilas post office opened on August 24, 1885, with James P. as its first postmaster.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/vilas_north_carolina",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Vilas sits about 5.6 miles west‑northwest of Boone along U.S. Route 421, keeping a rural feel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        12,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/vilas_north_carolina",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "At 2,746 feet, Vilas rises above Linville Creek, with surrounding peaks reaching roughly 3,400 feet.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/vilas_north_carolina",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Early settlers—Scotch‑Irish, English, and German—migrated from eastern North Carolina, Virginia, and Pennsylvania, farming corn, rye, and buckwheat.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
